Mechanisms
- app close::Intent::prepare captures actual Stage split path/ratios, tab/swarm and the UI restoration handle; no optimistic lifecycle mutation.
- IO Model.closes confirms only matching registry operation, generation and deadline. Metadata rebuilds prune/restore through the existing UI edits. The original sidebar order is restored too; a real three-PTY test caught the shared undo edit appending the row.
- A confirmed retained transition removes the grace row and emits exactly '<name> closed; its history is kept' once. No record/ring deletion.
- Retained close/undo hit regions come from the painted component layout; Cmd-Z is local once, Ctrl-Z remains PTY input, editor/launcher routes retain their keys.
- CloseSeat/UndoCloseSeat follow the existing admitted window relay and ctl_record journal; the window alone derives Position. ctl reports relayed, never claims restoration before metadata confirms it.
- ClosedStrip uses the shared retained kit, supplied remaining time and native token sources. Same Sidebar/SwarmCard extra-child port, no renderer/shader/pass addition.
- close::status(&model::Model, Instant) is a pure bounded readback: slots[{seat,swarm,tab}], grace[{seat,swarm,remaining_ms,undo}], notices[{swarm,text,time,truncated}], omitted and complete. No IO or second record reader. U1 AppStatus transport hookup remains for the accepted U1 union.

